WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.456
- My prom was kind of hilarious.

00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:04.345
I went with a very good guy friend of mine

00:00:04.345 --> 00:00:06.766
and another couple on a double date,

00:00:06.766 --> 00:00:09.574
and I actually made out with
the other guy's prom date.

00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:11.908
So technically, my prom was pretty great.

00:00:11.908 --> 00:00:13.623
(laughs)

00:00:13.623 --> 00:00:16.206
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.597 --> 00:00:27.654
- I never got to have a
prom, this is my first prom.

00:00:27.654 --> 00:00:29.120
- I went with a good friend of mine

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.713
who I was in school
with, and she and I used

00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:34.110
to like laugh constantly,
so we had a good time.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.119
And we matched, we were both
in like black featuring red.

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:40.015
- I definitely stood
out, I went to an all-boy

00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:43.764
Jesuit school in Miami,
where I was closeted

00:00:43.764 --> 00:00:47.563
because in the 90s that's
what you did in high school.

00:00:47.563 --> 00:00:49.813
- My prom was a lot of
fun, I just remember

00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:53.382
me and my friends renting
a limo and we just partied

00:00:53.382 --> 00:00:54.867
from the time we got in the limo

00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:57.612
to the time we got back
dropped off at home.

00:00:57.612 --> 00:00:58.903
- I had a good time, I danced a lot.

00:00:58.903 --> 00:00:59.981
- It felt very traditional, I feel.

00:00:59.981 --> 00:01:01.127
- It was definitely traditional.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.808
- We got like the corsages,
what are they called?

00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:05.545
- Corsages.
- Corsages.

00:01:05.545 --> 00:01:08.544
- Oh, I was prom king, I was very popular.

00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:10.248
I was captain of my
cheerleading squad, too.

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:12.325
- I actually did not attend prom.

00:01:12.325 --> 00:01:15.097
I didn't go because I didn't
really feel comfortable enough

00:01:15.097 --> 00:01:17.595
in my sexuality or my gender expression

00:01:17.595 --> 00:01:20.303
to really go to prom with
someone who I'd like to go with

00:01:20.303 --> 00:01:21.748
and what I wanted to wear.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.269
- I went to prom with a close
friend of mine who ended up

00:01:24.269 --> 00:01:27.209
dancing all night with a guy
that she liked, and you know,

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:28.997
I had a good time, but I ended up alone.

00:01:28.997 --> 00:01:30.295
- To prom, I went with a girl

00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:32.090
because it wasn't okay to be out.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.821
It was a great night,
but it wasn't a night

00:01:33.821 --> 00:01:35.498
where I was who I was fully.

00:01:35.498 --> 00:01:37.389
- [Robert Sepulveda Jr.]
I didn't go to prom.

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:38.661
- [Arisce] Aww.
- I didn't go to prom

00:01:38.661 --> 00:01:41.333
because I knew I was a gay boy

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:43.616
living in a very southern
city so when I heard

00:01:43.616 --> 00:01:45.894
that BuzzFeed was doing a queer prom,

00:01:45.894 --> 00:01:50.061
I thought that was the most
amazing, special thing on earth.

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:55.184
- Depending on where
these kids are located,

00:01:55.184 --> 00:01:57.802
there schools might not be
open to this kind of a thing

00:01:57.802 --> 00:01:59.733
and even if their schools
do have an open-door policy,

00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:01.119
they might not feel comfortable.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:03.015
So this is a safe space tonight.

00:02:03.015 --> 00:02:05.237
- I think it's so important for queer kids

00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:07.722
to see other queer kids
living authentically.

00:02:07.722 --> 00:02:10.700
To see all of these
LGBTQ+ people together,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.356
it really builds community
and I think that's something

00:02:13.356 --> 00:02:16.344
that LGBTQ young people
don't really get a lot of.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:19.011
I'm so, so happy to be you know,

00:02:20.585 --> 00:02:24.085
in this lifetime where we have queer proms

00:02:25.346 --> 00:02:28.240
and we have pride in high school.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.858
It's just an amazing thing so I love it.

00:02:30.858 --> 00:02:33.405
- I just think it's important,
in general, to get together

00:02:33.405 --> 00:02:34.959
and just celebrate who you are.

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:37.063
- It's so important to
express individuality

00:02:37.063 --> 00:02:39.123
and togetherness at the same time,

00:02:39.123 --> 00:02:41.498
especially in this political climate.

00:02:41.498 --> 00:02:42.331
- [Scott] And it's so unbelievable

00:02:42.331 --> 00:02:43.318
that one of the biggest websites

00:02:43.318 --> 00:02:45.406
in the world, BuzFeed,
is putting on an event

00:02:45.406 --> 00:02:48.012
that's just completely
inclusive of queer kids

00:02:48.012 --> 00:02:49.488
and so all of these people around America

00:02:49.488 --> 00:02:51.014
and around the world
are seeing these videos

00:02:51.014 --> 00:02:52.970
and they are thinking, wow, I'm not alone.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.163
Things like this are happening.

00:02:54.163 --> 00:02:56.091
- When I grew up, I didn't
have anything like this.

00:02:56.091 --> 00:02:57.930
I didn't have this kind of visibility,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.156
to see and to feel the support.

00:03:00.156 --> 00:03:02.554
- There's like a box
of like, typical prom.

00:03:02.554 --> 00:03:05.271
So to see something like this
would have been really cool.

00:03:05.271 --> 00:03:07.288
Like you would have had ideas
and just felt empowered.

00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:10.022
- To show up to your peers
wearing whatever you want.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.631
- Prom is usually just a cisgender,

00:03:11.631 --> 00:03:13.800
heteronormative tradition.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.255
- Times are changing so much
and it's beautiful to see kids

00:03:16.255 --> 00:03:17.742
be able to celebrate who they are

00:03:17.742 --> 00:03:19.295
in the fullness of who they are.

00:03:19.295 --> 00:03:21.354
- I think the last thing you
want to be thinking about

00:03:21.354 --> 00:03:22.538
is, are you allowed to go there

00:03:22.538 --> 00:03:24.494
because you choose to
go with who you like,

00:03:24.494 --> 00:03:26.229
who you love, you know,
so I think it's important

00:03:26.229 --> 00:03:28.251
to have events like this
to raise awareness that

00:03:28.251 --> 00:03:30.349
this is something we're
not going to tolerate

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:32.153
in this society, that
America's better than this.

00:03:32.153 --> 00:03:35.070
That people are the same and equal.

00:03:37.151 --> 00:03:39.129
- My queerest story.

00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:40.616
- Oh some mini girl

00:03:40.616 --> 00:03:42.320
(laughter)

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.289
Okay, that's maybe a little too dirty.

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:45.971
- Two years ago at the Grammys,

00:03:45.971 --> 00:03:47.868
he wore like a full dress moment.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.754
- I did wear a dress to the Grammys.

00:03:49.754 --> 00:03:51.628
- And it was bold and it was beautiful

00:03:51.628 --> 00:03:53.249
and he got all raving reviews.

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:57.674
- I was once in hug with Ellen
DeGeneres and Ellen Paige.

00:03:57.674 --> 00:04:02.557
I don't know if it gets any
queerer than that or awesome.

00:04:02.557 --> 00:04:05.463
- I got to open Brittney
Spears' Circus Tour,

00:04:05.463 --> 00:04:06.926
that's pretty major.

00:04:06.926 --> 00:04:09.540
- So opening for Kesha at my first Pride

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.796
felt pretty queer and pretty amazing.

00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:17.090
- I was partially raised by a
member of the LGBTQ community.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.633
I'm straight but I've always
kind of been put in that box.

00:04:20.633 --> 00:04:22.721
I feel like I definitely connect

00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:25.302
and understand what the experience is.

00:04:25.302 --> 00:04:27.842
- Honestly when I started to
get into glitter on my face,

00:04:27.842 --> 00:04:30.188
like probably in the last year

00:04:30.188 --> 00:04:32.059
or actually a few months actually.

00:04:32.059 --> 00:04:33.800
- [Adam] Oh I'm just
all queer all the time.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.691
I mean, I don't know
if you can classify one

00:04:35.691 --> 00:04:37.480
as being more queer than the other.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.647
I'm like a unicorn, you can't
see the horn, it's invisible.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.772
- You are not wrong, period.

00:04:48.772 --> 00:04:51.319
You're not wrong and
don't ever let anybody

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:53.365
make you feel wrong for just being you.

00:04:53.365 --> 00:04:56.056
- [Arisce] Keep resisting
and keep being yourself,

00:04:56.056 --> 00:04:57.440
regardless of what people tell you to do

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.331
because society is really good at saying,

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:01.197
oh be yourself, oh
wait, but not like that.

00:05:01.197 --> 00:05:02.710
Enough of that shit, be yourself.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.237
And shove it in people's faces.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.901
- When your at home as a
teenager dealing with bullying

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:09.263
or with difficult people, I
would say that it's important

00:05:09.263 --> 00:05:10.783
to stay true to yourself.

00:05:10.783 --> 00:05:14.203
- The community is much larger
than we think it is at times.

00:05:14.203 --> 00:05:16.414
I remember growing up and
feeling like it's this big.

00:05:16.414 --> 00:05:19.524
And once you kind of
make these connections,

00:05:19.524 --> 00:05:20.974
it kind of opens that up.

00:05:20.974 --> 00:05:24.285
- [Echo] The people who matter don't care

00:05:24.285 --> 00:05:27.123
and the people who care don't matter.

00:05:27.123 --> 00:05:28.981
- I think if anybody's out
there and they feel like

00:05:28.981 --> 00:05:32.900
they don't belong at prom,
prove all those kids wrong.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.598
Find a crew to go with,
go with your friends,

00:05:34.598 --> 00:05:37.732
go with a date, I know it's
hard, and I know high school

00:05:37.732 --> 00:05:41.269
makes it very difficult,
but if your at a dance,

00:05:41.269 --> 00:05:45.705
it's your memory, it's not
their memory so do it for you.

00:05:45.705 --> 00:05:48.276
- [Deray] You belong everywhere
and sometimes the prom,

00:05:48.276 --> 00:05:50.865
in some places, isn't just
the best place for you.

00:05:50.865 --> 00:05:52.879
Which you can make that
experience somewhere else

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:55.128
and it doesn't have to be
at the school or in the gym.

00:05:55.128 --> 00:05:56.502
- You have something to give.

00:05:56.502 --> 00:05:58.195
You have something to offer this world.

00:05:58.195 --> 00:06:00.807
- It definitely gets better
and just try to enjoy it.

00:06:00.807 --> 00:06:03.741
And I would say just be
yourself, like no shame.

00:06:03.741 --> 00:06:05.410
Just be yourself.
- Absolutely.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.533
- Have fun and live your life,

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:07.641
you only get one chance at this

00:06:07.641 --> 00:06:09.542
and you have to do it your way.

00:06:09.542 --> 00:06:12.125
(upbeat music)

